==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkʁøːtə/|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|krotte}}, {{m|gmh|kröte}}, {{m|gmh|krete|krëte}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|chrota}}, {{m|goh|krota}}, {{m|goh|kreta||toad}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*krudō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*kredō||toad}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*guredʰ-||toad}}. Cognate with {{cog|gml|krode|krōde|toad}}, dated Dutch {{m|nl|krodde||toad}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Kröten}}

# [[toad]]

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-f|n}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|de|Schildkröte}}
* {{l|de|Krötenwanderung}}

====See also====
* {{l|de|Frosch|g=m}}
* {{l|de|Kaulquappe|g=f}}

===Etymology 2===
Probably a humorous [[malapropism]] of {{etyl|nds-de|de}} {{m|nds-de|Groten}}, from {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|grōten}}. Compare German {{m|de|Groschen}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Kröten}}

# {{lb|de|informal|chiefly|plural}} [[money]]

